How to Install the NC State VPN Client


NC State provides a virtual private network (VPN) connection through the Cisco Secure Client software. A VPN connection is typically required when accessing sensitive information or using on-campus resources from an off-campus connection.


Install Cisco Secure Client
To download and install Cisco Secure Client on your computer, select your operating system or device below and follow the provided instructions.
Install the NC State VPN Client for Windows 10 and 11
Installation instructions for Windows 10 and 11
1. Download the Cisco Secure Client 5.X installer.
2. Double click on the downloaded file to begin the installation.
3. Accept the End User License Agreement.
4. Click on the Install button.
5. If you are prompted, allow the application to make changes on your computer.
The Cisco Secure Client will be added to your Start menu.
Install the NC State VPN Client for Windows Running on ARM Processors
Installation instructions for Windows on ARM
1. Download the Cisco Secure Client 5.X installer.
2. Double click on the downloaded file to begin the installation.
3. Accept the End User License Agreement.
4. Click on the Install button.
5. If you are prompted, allow the application to make changes on your computer.
The Cisco Secure Client will be added to your Start menu.
Install the NC State VPN Client for macOS 13 and higher
Cisco Secure Client VPN Installation Instructions for macOS
1. Download the Secure Client 5.X installer for macOS
2. Double-click to open the cisco-secure-client-macos-5.1.16.194-predeploy-k9.dmg file.
3. Double-click the Cisco Secure Client.pkg icon.
4. Click the Continue button on the Introduction and License Agreement screens.
5. Click Agree to the terms of the software license agreement.
6. In the Destination Select window, choose the disk where you want to install the software if prompted, and click Continue.
7. In the Installation Type window, UNCHECK EVERYTHING except AnyConnect VPN, click Continue, and click Install.

  

8. In the Installation window, authorize the installation on your computer by entering your Mac login info.
9. Click on the Close button once you see that the installation was successful.
   * You can choose to Keep or Move to Trash the Cisco Secure Client installer.
Install and Connect to the NC State VPN on Linux
Install OpenConnect Client
   1. Open a Terminal window.
   2. Enter the command:
   3. sudo apt-get -y install openconnect network-manager-openconnect network-manager-openconnect-gnome
   4. Enter your administrator password when prompted.
   5. Wait for the packages to finish installing.
Set Up the NC State VPN Connection
   1. Select the Network icon in the upper-right.
   2. Open the Network Settings.
   3. Select the + icon next to the VPN Heading.
   4. Select Multi-Protocol VPN Client.
   1. Name: NC State VPN (or any other meaningful name)
   2. VPN Protocol: Cisco AnyConnect or openconnect
   3. Gateway: vpn.ncsu.edu
   5. All other settings can be left as provided.
   6. Select Add in the top right.
Install the NC State VPN Client on an iPhone or iPad
Installation Instructions for iPhone or iPad
   1. Install the Cisco Secure Client-AnyConnect app from the App Store.
   2. Open the AnyConnect app.
   3. Select Connections, followed by selecting Add VPN Connection...
   4. Enter vpn.ncsu.edu into the Server Address field and select Save.
   5. You can enter a description, but it is not required.
   6. Select Allow when asked, "AnyConnect" Would like to add VPN Configurations.
   7. Enter your iPhone's PIN or passcode to authorize adding the VPN configuration.
   8. Tap Back.
   9. Toggle the switch to the right of AnyConnect VPN.
Install and Connect to the NC State VPN Client for Android 4.0 or Newer
Installation Instructions for Android
   1. Install the Cisco Secure Client-AnyConnect app from the Google Play Store.
   2. Open the AnyConnect/Cisco Secure Client app on your Android device.
   3. Select Connections and tap the plus (+) icon in the lower-right corner
   4. Enter vpn.ncsu.edu into the Server Address field and select Done.
   1. You can enter a description, but it is not required.
   5. Tap the ← in the top-left corner to return to the starting screen.
   6. Toggle the switch to the right of AnyConnect VPN.
